{"notes":"SETTLED: 1) Score: 1 per exact block, 0.25 if only colour or only shape matches, divided by the taller tower's height. Max 8 words, 16-word list only. 2) Colour words: kano=red, fuza=yellow, nove=blue, muva=orange, vonu=green, tumu=purple. Each colour word builds one block, and the block is a star by default. 3) Round with the new partner: message kano tumu nove fuza tumu tumu kano kano, which is 8 colour words, built 8 stars, so every word is a colour block when the sender uses only colours. Colours were all right, shapes all wrong (targets were cubes and rings). Score 0.34 because only the colour matched on most blocks, plus one exact star. 4) Earlier partner: vepu after a colour seemed to be cone, but this is unconfirmed and the partner may have been different. Do not rely on suffix theory; the builder may build any non-colour word as a star or ignore it. 5) Targets over 8 blocks lose the last blocks to the word cap. 6) Colour-only baseline gives about 0.35-0.65.

OPEN: 1) Shape words for ring, ball, cube, cone are still unknown. Candidates: fidi, kuru, neto, loku, dobo, zeki, tido, mape, melu, vepu. 2) Whether shape words are suffixes or take their own block position with the new partner. 3) Whether a shape word is worth one of the 8 word slots. 4) The new partner may use different conventions, but the colour words seemed to be shared.

NEXT: 1) As sender on short targets (4 blocks or fewer), test one shape word directly after a colour, such as kano fidi, and see what gets built. 2) On long targets use plain colours in order, one word per block. 3) As builder, read colours by the list, build each colour word as a star block, and treat an unlisted word after a colour as a possible shape hint: if it follows a colour, add no extra block unless the message needs it for height. 4) Keep messages to 8 words or fewer and record what the shown target reveals about each shape word."}

{"notes":"SETTLED: 1) Score: 1 per exact block, 0.25 if only colour or only shape matches, divided by the taller tower's height. Max 8 words, 16-word list only. 2) Colour words: kano=red, fuza=yellow, nove=blue, muva=orange, vonu=green, tumu=purple. Reliable across partners. Builders build one block per colour word, in order, and default to stars. 3) kuru, melu, fidi, loku, vepu give no block and no shape effect; treat as filler. 4) Colour-only messages give all stars: about 0.25 per block on non-star targets, 1 per block on star targets, so about 0.36-0.45 overall. Targets over 8 blocks lose last blocks to the word cap. 5) Repeated colour words make same-colour runs. 6) NEW: neto after a colour word (kano neto kano neto) did NOT make cubes; the builder made red star, red star (0.25). So neto looks like filler or is unknown to this partner; it does not produce a block or a cube.

OPEN: 1) No shape word is proven. Words for ring, ball, cube, cone unknown. Candidates left: dobo, zeki, tido, mape (neto weak, probably no effect). 2) Shape word position unclear; may need to go right after its colour word, or before it. 3) Whether builders ignore all non-colour words. 4) Whether any partner knows shape words at all; maybe shapes cannot be signalled and stars are the only reachable shape. 5) How to split word budget on long targets.

NEXT: 1) As sender on a short target (3-5 blocks), test one candidate (dobo, zeki, tido or mape) per round directly after the colour word, e.g. kano dobo, and compare with star default. Record result. 2) On star-heavy targets, one colour word per block, repeated for runs, no shape words. 3) As builder, one block per colour word, default to stars; if a candidate word follows a colour word, try a non-star shape for it and note the target. 4) Record every shape-word result after each round. 5) Don't use vepu, kuru, melu, fidi, loku, or neto except as filler."}
